-- Steal Breaks — Reading the Pitcher & First Move  [Baserunning]  → READY
-- source: description expanded into setup and execution from the existing cues, which already set out the tells and the charted jumps
UPDATE public.drill_resources SET
  description = 'Practising the jump itself, separately from the sprint. Runners take a primary lead against a pitcher working from the stretch and break on the first movement toward home. A coach charts every repetition as a good jump, a late one, or a pickoff. One pitcher tell is taught at a time — the heel lifting, the front shoulder leaning, the head turning — because a runner watching for three tells is watching for none. The sprint hardly matters here; the half-second of recognition is the whole skill.',
  regression_notes = 'Have the pitcher exaggerate one tell and announce what to watch for. Recognising a signposted move is the step before spotting a subtle one.',
  progression_notes = 'Stop announcing the tell, add genuine pickoff attempts, and time first-move-to-second so the jump becomes a number that can improve.',
  practice_roles = ARRAY['isolate', 'decision']::text[],
  updated_at = now()
WHERE id = 'f9d5d796-ce11-4964-bc70-a3ce5f8a607f';

-- Pro Base-Stealing Package — Leads, Reads & Jumps  [Baserunning]  → READY
-- source: description expanded into setup and execution from the existing cues, which already set out the live pitcher, the charting and the one-tell-at-a-time method
UPDATE public.drill_resources SET
  description = 'The complete stealing package against a live pitcher from the stretch: how far to take the primary lead, which pitcher tells to read, and how to convert the read into a jump. Eight to ten live repetitions, every one charted as safe, late or picked off. One tell is introduced per session. First-move-to-second is timed so improvement is visible rather than asserted. This is the advanced end of the category and it assumes the secondary lead is already automatic.',
  regression_notes = 'Drop the live pitcher for a coach making an exaggerated move, and remove the pickoff threat. The read is learnable without the consequence attached.',
  progression_notes = 'Add left-handed pitchers, which is a different read entirely, and run it inside a scrimmage where the runner chooses whether to go at all.',
  reps_guidance = '8-10 live steal reps, charted',
  practice_roles = ARRAY['progress', 'decision']::text[],
  updated_at = now()
WHERE id = '4106c25c-beeb-4d11-b1aa-eb9aa85978ae';

-- Pop-Up Slide — Slide and Advance  [Baserunning]  → READY
-- source: description expanded into setup and execution from the existing cues, which already set out the slide-through-the-bag momentum and the overthrow read
UPDATE public.drill_resources SET
  description = 'The slide that finishes standing up. The runner slides bent-leg into the bag, but rather than stopping there, the momentum carries them up onto the planted foot so they finish on their feet facing the next base. A coach throws a simulated overthrow on the last few repetitions so the runner has to find the ball and decide whether to advance. Eight to ten slides, the last four with an overthrow read. It only works once the basic bent-leg slide is automatic.',
  regression_notes = 'Go back to the basic bent-leg slide on grass or a mat, without popping up. A runner who is still thinking about the slide cannot also read a throw.',
  progression_notes = 'Slide at full speed on dirt, and make the overthrow read live rather than simulated, so the decision to advance carries a real risk of being out.',
  reps_guidance = '8-10 pop-up slides, last 4 with an overthrow read',
  updated_at = now()
WHERE id = '9335a346-33a3-4bd1-b65c-2664f9c7fcfb';

-- Sliding Practice Stations  [Baserunning]  → READY
-- source: description expanded into setup and execution from the existing cues, which already set out the rotating stations and the left/right call
UPDATE public.drill_resources SET
  description = 'Sliding volume for a whole team without anyone getting dirt burn. Set two or three sliding lanes on grass or on mats, each with a loose base, and rotate small groups through them as a station during practice. Two rounds of six to eight slides per station. Because the surface is forgiving, players get far more repetitions than they would on the infield, and a coach pointing left or right as they approach adds the choice of which side of the bag to slide to.',
  regression_notes = 'One lane, straight slides only, from a jog. The volume is the point and volume at a walk is still volume.',
  progression_notes = 'Add the left/right call, then move to a dirt surface, then run slides at the end of a full-speed baserunning circuit where the legs are already tired.',
  reps_guidance = '2 rounds of 6-8 slides per station',
  practice_roles = ARRAY['repetition']::text[],
  updated_at = now()
WHERE id = '282be624-51e9-4a06-ab37-7646b0a3da8b';

-- Bent-Leg Slide Basics — The Right Way to Slide  [Baserunning]  → READY
-- source: description expanded into setup and execution from the existing cues, which already set out the figure-4 tuck, the grass-first rule and the marked start line
UPDATE public.drill_resources SET
  description = 'The first sliding lesson, taught somewhere soft. On grass in socks or on a sliding mat, the runner starts from a walk, sits into the slide, tucks one leg under the other into a figure-four, and keeps both hands up in the air. Mark a start line about two body lengths from the base so the slide begins at the right distance rather than on top of the bag. Walk, then jog, then run. Ten to fifteen slides, and nobody goes near dirt on day one.',
  regression_notes = 'Sit and slide from a standing start on a wet mat, with no approach at all. The figure-four shape is the whole first lesson and the run-up can wait.',
  progression_notes = 'Build to full speed on grass, then to dirt, then to the pop-up slide. Never move a player on who is still landing on their knees.',
  reps_guidance = '10-15 slides per session, building speed gradually',
  updated_at = now()
WHERE id = 'b610bf25-fbc7-46e3-9c8a-16e07224bf70';

-- One-Knee Receiving — Advanced Framing Setup  [Catching]  → READY
-- source: description expanded into setup and execution from the existing cues, which already set out the drill count, the free-leg check and the gradual speed increase
UPDATE public.drill_resources SET
  description = 'Receiving from the one-knee-down stance, for catchers who have outgrown the two-knee setup. The catcher drops the throwing-side knee, keeps the free leg positioned so a block or a throw is still possible, and receives pitches with the glove working up into the zone rather than dropping under the ball. Four sets of ten receives per setup — glove-side low, arm-side low, and the edges. Machine work is ideal because the volume matters and the location has to repeat.',
  regression_notes = 'Go back to the two-knee setup and get the glove path right there first. The one-knee stance is a ceiling, not a starting point, and it makes a bad receiver look worse.',
  progression_notes = 'Increase pitch velocity gradually, then add blocking and throw-downs from the same stance so the free-leg position has to survive a real play.',
  reps_guidance = '4 sets of 10 receives per setup (RH low, LH low, edges)',
  practice_roles = ARRAY['isolate', 'progress']::text[],
  updated_at = now()
WHERE id = '478cb186-6370-494d-b94a-47136344ccd8';

